window.WONDER_READY_POSTS = [{"id":"wp-script-6","ideaId":6,"week":1,"date":"2026-10-12","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Nobody told me this before I tried cloth pads, so I'm telling you now.","title":"Nobody told me this before I tried cloth pads, so I'm telling you now.","caption":"Nobody told me this before I tried cloth pads, so I'm telling you now.\n\nMost of what puts people off is what nobody explains up front: that you can go slowly, that the first pad you try may need a tweak, and that washing is far less dramatic than it sounds. Swipe through for the things I wish more people knew.\n\nIf you're curious but unsure where to begin, send a message to @ecoclothpad and we'll work it out together, one pad at a time.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #PeriodTalk #BeginnerFriendly","notes":"If you have your own 'first time' memory, add one line of it to the caption.","confirmation":"","script":"Slide 1 (cover): What I wish more people knew before trying cloth pads.\nSlide 2: You don't have to switch everything in one go. Most people start with one pad on one easy day, and that is a perfectly good beginning.\nSlide 3: Your first pad might not be your forever pad. Flow, length and fabric are personal, so it can take a try or two to find the one that feels like yours.\nSlide 4: Washing is simpler than it sounds. A cold rinse, a wash following your pad's care instructions and a proper dry is most of the story.\nSlide 5: A leak can mean the fit, absorbency or changing routine needs adjusting. Notice where and when it happens, then try one change at a time.\nSlide 6: Comfort is the surprise. Soft fabric against your skin makes a bigger difference than you'd expect.\nSlide 7: Keeping cloth and disposable pads in the same drawer is completely fine. Reusable is a choice, not a test you can fail.\nSlide 8: Curious? Start small and ask me anything. Message @ecoclothpad and we'll find your first pad together.","slides":[{"title":"What I wish more people knew before trying cloth pads.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"You don't have to switch everything in one go. Most people start with one pad on one easy day, and that is a perfectly good beginning."},{"title":"02","body":"Your first pad might not be your forever pad. Flow, length and fabric are personal, so it can take a try or two to find the one that feels like yours."},{"title":"03","body":"Washing is simpler than it sounds. A cold rinse, a wash following your pad's care instructions and a proper dry is most of the story."},{"title":"04","body":"A leak can mean the fit, absorbency or changing routine needs adjusting. Notice where and when it happens, then try one change at a time."},{"title":"05","body":"Comfort is the surprise. Soft fabric against your skin makes a bigger difference than you'd expect."},{"title":"06","body":"Keeping cloth and disposable pads in the same drawer is completely fine. Reusable is a choice, not a test you can fail."},{"title":"Save this before you start","body":"Start small, at your own pace. Follow @ecoclothpad for practical cloth pad tips."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-125","ideaId":125,"week":1,"date":"2026-10-14","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Hi, I'm Nilam, and every pad you see here goes through my hands.","title":"Hi, I'm Nilam, and every pad you see here goes through my hands.","caption":"Hi, I'm Nilam, and every pad you see here goes through my hands.\n\nI choose the fabrics, cutting, layering, stitching and packing each order myself. It's a small, home-based business, which means your pad is made with real attention and can be made to suit you.\n\nIf there's something you've always wanted to ask about cloth pads, ask away in the comments. I read every one.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #MeetTheMaker #HandmadeInSingapore #ClothPadsSingapore #SmallBusinessSG","notes":"Use a photo of you at the sewing machine.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Hi, I'm Nilam. / Every Wonder Pad is made by hand, by me in Singapore.","slides":[],"imageText":"Hi, I'm Nilam. / Every Wonder Pad is made by hand, by me in Singapore."},{"id":"wp-script-114","ideaId":114,"week":1,"date":"2026-10-16","format":"Reel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Same pads. Same week. Completely different periods.","title":"Same pads. Same week. Completely different periods.","caption":"Same pads. Same week. Completely different periods.\n\nTwo people can follow the same routine and need completely different protection. Length, absorbency and shape are not the same thing, and what suits one body won't suit the next.\n\nSend this to a friend whose period is nothing like yours, and tell me in the comments what your flow is like.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #PeriodTalk #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #YourFlowYourPad","notes":"Record with text on screen; a voiceover is optional. 'It took me ages to realise' is written as your voice; change it if it isn't true for you.","confirmation":"","script":"Length: 20 to 25 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: Two pads side by side on the pink background.\nOn screen: We've been using the same pads.\nVoiceover: We've been using the same pads...\nScene 2\nShot: Same shot, one pad slides to the left.\nOn screen: But we don't have the same period.\nVoiceover: ...but we don't have the same period.\nScene 3\nShot: Hand points to the longer pad, then the shorter one.\nOn screen: One of us needs more length. / One of us needs more absorbency.\nVoiceover: One of us needs a longer pad. The other one needs more absorbency. And neither of us was wrong.\nScene 4\nShot: Pads rest together; text appears in handwriting.\nOn screen: Your flow is yours.\nVoiceover: That's why one pad was never going to fit everyone.\nScene 5\nShot: Final shot of @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Tell me about your flow. I'll help you find your pad.\nVoiceover: Tell me what your flow is like, and I'll help you find yours.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-8","ideaId":8,"week":1,"date":"2026-10-18","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"You don't have to throw out every disposable pad tomorrow.","title":"You don't have to throw out every disposable pad tomorrow.","caption":"You don't have to throw out every disposable pad tomorrow.\n\nStart with one cloth pad on a day you're at home. See how it feels, how it washes and how it fits into your week. Then try another day, or a different length. Some people use cloth only at home, some only overnight, and some a mix of everything. All of it counts.\n\nReusable is something you can build up slowly. What would your first step be? Tell me in the comments.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #SlowSwitch #PeriodCare","notes":"","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: You don't have to switch everything at once.","slides":[],"imageText":"You don't have to switch everything at once."},{"id":"wp-script-12","ideaId":12,"week":2,"date":"2026-10-19","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"The pad that saved your friend might not be the one for you.","title":"The pad that saved your friend might not be the one for you.","caption":"The pad that saved your friend might not be the one for you.\n\nSo many of us grew up assuming one size and one type of pad would do the job for everyone. But flow, body shape, lifestyle and comfort all differ, and the right pad is the one made for yours.\n\nSwipe through to see how to start working out what you need. If you'd like a hand, message @ecoclothpad.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #CustomPads #PeriodTalk #ReusablePads","notes":"","confirmation":"","script":"Slide 1 (cover): The pad that saved your friend might not be the one for you.\nSlide 2: Two friends can use the exact same pad and have two completely different experiences. It's not that one of you is doing it wrong.\nSlide 3: Flow is different for everyone. Some people have a few heavy days and a long light tail, while others have an even flow from start to finish.\nSlide 4: Your body and your day matter too. Sitting at a desk, walking around Singapore or sleeping through the night each ask something different of a pad.\nSlide 5: Length and absorbency are not the same thing. Length is about coverage, and absorbency is about how much a pad can hold.\nSlide 6: So start by noticing, not guessing. Where does it leak, how long can you wear it comfortably, and what feels right against your skin?\nSlide 7: That's exactly why I make custom pads. You choose the length, the shape and the absorbency, and the fabric is the fun part.\nSlide 8: Tell me what your days are like and I'll help you pick. Message @ecoclothpad to start.","slides":[{"title":"The pad that saved your friend might not be the one for you.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"Two friends can use the exact same pad and have two completely different experiences. It's not that one of you is doing it wrong."},{"title":"02","body":"Flow is different for everyone. Some people have a few heavy days and a long light tail, while others have an even flow from start to finish."},{"title":"03","body":"Your body and your day matter too. Sitting at a desk, walking around Singapore or sleeping through the night each ask something different of a pad."},{"title":"04","body":"Length and absorbency are not the same thing. Length is about coverage, and absorbency is about how much a pad can hold."},{"title":"05","body":"So start by noticing, not guessing. Where does it leak, how long can you wear it comfortably, and what feels right against your skin?"},{"title":"06","body":"That's exactly why I make custom pads. You choose the length, the shape and the absorbency, and the fabric is the fun part."},{"title":"Save this before choosing your next pad","body":"Notice your flow, fit and routine. Message @ecoclothpad if you would like help choosing."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-115","ideaId":115,"week":2,"date":"2026-10-21","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Your flow is yours. Your pad should be too.","title":"Your flow is yours. Your pad should be too.","caption":"Your flow is yours. Your pad should be too.\n\nNo two periods are the same, so why would we expect one pad to suit every body? That's the idea behind everything I make here: pads that start with you and your needs, and then get a beautiful fabric on top.\n\nTag a friend whose flow is nothing like yours.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #YourFlowYourPad #ClothPadsSingapore #CustomPads #PeriodPositive","notes":"Use a close-up of a favourite fabric on the brand pink background, with the line in Kalam.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Your flow is yours. / Your pad should be too.","slides":[],"imageText":"Your flow is yours. / Your pad should be too."},{"id":"wp-script-14","ideaId":14,"week":2,"date":"2026-10-23","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Yes, cloth pads can handle a heavy flow. Here's how.","title":"Yes, cloth pads can handle a heavy flow. Here's how.","caption":"Yes, cloth pads can handle a heavy flow. Here's how.\n\nThe secret isn't a magic fabric. It's choosing the right absorbency, the right length and a changing routine that fits your flow. Once those three line up, heavy days feel a lot more manageable.\n\nIf your flow feels very heavy or has changed suddenly, it's always worth speaking to a doctor as well.\n\nMessage @ecoclothpad your flow and I'll help you find the right pad.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #HeavyFlow #ReusablePads #PeriodCare","notes":"Add your own heavy-flow pad names or sizes to slide 3 or 4 if you want it to be product-specific.","confirmation":"Confirm your heavy-flow pad options and absorbency guidance.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Yes, cloth pads can handle a heavy flow. Here's how.\nSlide 2: A heavy flow needs a pad built for it. Thin, light pads won't do the job, but a pad with more absorbent layers can.\nSlide 3: Choose absorbency first. Pick a pad that's made for heavy days rather than stretching a light one further than it was meant to go.\nSlide 4: Then think about length. A longer pad covers more at the front and the back, which is where many leaks start.\nSlide 5: Change on your own rhythm. A heavy day may mean changing more often, so don't wait until a pad is completely full.\nSlide 6: Pack a spare and a small wet bag. Then a change when you're out is easy, and you can carry on with your day.\nSlide 7: For overnight, go longer and snug, so the pad stays where you want it while you move around.\nSlide 8: Not sure what your heavy day really needs? Message @ecoclothpad your flow and we'll build a pad around it.","slides":[{"title":"Yes, cloth pads can handle a heavy flow. Here's how.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"A heavy flow needs a pad built for it. Thin, light pads won't do the job, but a pad with more absorbent layers can."},{"title":"02","body":"Choose absorbency first. Pick a pad that's made for heavy days rather than stretching a light one further than it was meant to go."},{"title":"03","body":"Then think about length. A longer pad covers more at the front and the back, which is where many leaks start."},{"title":"04","body":"Change your pad regularly, and sooner when your flow requires it. You do not need to wait until it is completely full."},{"title":"05","body":"Pack a spare and a small wet bag. Then a change when you're out is easy, and you can carry on with your day."},{"title":"06","body":"For overnight, go longer and snug, so the pad stays where you want it while you move around."},{"title":"Need help choosing for heavy days?","body":"Message @ecoclothpad about pad options. Very heavy or suddenly changed bleeding is worth discussing with a doctor."}],"cta":"message"},{"id":"wp-script-104","ideaId":104,"week":2,"date":"2026-10-25","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"My fabric stash has officially taken over the sewing room.","title":"My fabric stash has officially taken over the sewing room.","caption":"My fabric stash has officially taken over the sewing room.\n\nEvery time I tell myself I have enough, a print I can't live without turns up. This is my never-ending collection of fabrics, and some of them are waiting for the right customer to come along and claim them.\n\nShow me your own stash in the comments. Fabric, yarn, books or anything else. I won't judge.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #FabricHoarder #SewingRoom #HandmadeInSingapore #MakerLife","notes":"Take a wide, slightly messy photo of your fabric shelves or boxes.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: My fabric stash has officially taken over the sewing room.","slides":[],"imageText":"My fabric stash has officially taken over the sewing room."},{"id":"wp-script-26","ideaId":26,"week":3,"date":"2026-10-26","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Longer isn't always safer. Here's what actually stops a leak.","title":"Longer isn't always safer. Here's what actually stops a leak.","caption":"Longer isn't always safer. Here's what actually stops a leak.\n\nIt's one of the most common mix-ups I see. Length decides coverage, absorbency decides capacity, and a good pad needs both to suit your flow and your body.\n\nSave this before your next order, and send me a message if you'd like help choosing.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #CustomPads #ReusablePads #PeriodTalk","notes":"","confirmation":"","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Longer isn't always safer. Here's what actually stops a leak.\nSlide 2: It's easy to assume that a longer pad is a stronger pad. But length and absorbency are two different things.\nSlide 3: Length is coverage. It decides how much of you the pad protects, front to back.\nSlide 4: Absorbency is capacity. It's about how much liquid the pad can hold before it needs changing.\nSlide 5: A very long pad with light absorbency can still leak on a heavy day. A shorter pad with the right absorbency can be perfect on others.\nSlide 6: Fit and shape matter as well. A pad that shifts or bunches won't protect as well as one that sits comfortably in place.\nSlide 7: So when you choose, ask two questions: how much coverage do I need, and how much can it hold?\nSlide 8: Not sure about your answers? Message @ecoclothpad and I'll help you work them out.","slides":[{"title":"Longer isn't always safer. Here's what actually stops a leak.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"It's easy to assume that a longer pad is a stronger pad. But length and absorbency are two different things."},{"title":"02","body":"Length is coverage. It decides how much of you the pad protects, front to back."},{"title":"03","body":"Absorbency is capacity. It's about how much liquid the pad can hold before it needs changing."},{"title":"04","body":"A very long pad with light absorbency can still leak on a heavy day. A shorter pad with the right absorbency can be perfect on others."},{"title":"05","body":"Fit and shape matter as well. A pad that shifts or bunches won't protect as well as one that sits comfortably in place."},{"title":"06","body":"So when you choose, ask two questions: how much coverage do I need, and how much can it hold?"},{"title":"Save this before your next order","body":"Coverage and absorbency do different jobs. Keep this guide handy when you choose."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-108","ideaId":108,"week":3,"date":"2026-10-28","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Choosing fabric for someone else's pads is my favourite part of the job.","title":"Choosing fabric for someone else's pads is my favourite part of the job.","caption":"Choosing fabric for someone else's pads is my favourite part of the job.\n\nWhen a customer tells me what they love, I get to lay out prints and colours and imagine them using something that was made just for them. It never gets old.\n\nIf you're thinking about a custom set, send a message to @ecoclothpad and I'll help you pick your prints.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #CustomPads #HandmadeInSingapore #ClothPadsSingapore #FabricLove","notes":"Show the fabrics only. Don't include customer names, chats or photos.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Choosing fabrics for someone else's pads is my favourite part of the job.","slides":[],"imageText":"Choosing fabrics for someone else's pads is my favourite part of the job."},{"id":"wp-script-27","ideaId":27,"week":3,"date":"2026-10-30","format":"Reel","effort":"Heavy","hook":"Here's how a custom Wonder Pad goes from your WhatsApp message to your door.","title":"Here's how a custom Wonder Pad goes from your WhatsApp message to your door.","caption":"Here's how a custom Wonder Pad goes from your WhatsApp message to your door.\n\nIt starts with a conversation about your flow and your day. Then you choose fabric, length, shape and absorbency, and I make it by hand.\n\nThis is what makes custom different from standard: it's built around you, not the average. If you'd like to start yours, message @ecoclothpad.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #CustomPads #HowItsMade #ClothPadsSingapore #HandmadeInSingapore","notes":"Adjust the steps to match your real process (for example how payment, delivery and timing work) before filming. Blur or avoid any customer names. Use a staged conversation rather than a real customer chat.","confirmation":"","script":"Length: 25 to 30 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: Phone screen: a staged demonstration message, with no real customer information.\nOn screen: Step 1: You message me.\nVoiceover: Here's how a custom Wonder Pad gets made. It starts with a message.\nScene 2\nShot: Fabric swatches fanned out on the table.\nOn screen: Step 2: Pick your fabric.\nVoiceover: You pick your fabric, and this is the fun part.\nScene 3\nShot: Two or three pads of different lengths and shapes.\nOn screen: Step 3: Choose length, shape and absorbency.\nVoiceover: Then we choose the length, shape and absorbency that suit your flow.\nScene 4\nShot: Cutting, layering and stitching close-ups.\nOn screen: Step 4: I make it by hand.\nVoiceover: Then I cut, layer and stitch it, by hand, at home.\nScene 5\nShot: Pads being wrapped and packed.\nOn screen: Step 5: Packed with care.\nVoiceover: I pack it up carefully...\nScene 6\nShot: Finished pad held up to the camera.\nOn screen: Made for you.\nVoiceover: ...and it arrives made for your body, your flow and your style.\nScene 7\nShot: Your Instagram handle: @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Message me to start yours.\nVoiceover: Message me on WhatsApp when you're ready to start.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-30","ideaId":30,"week":3,"date":"2026-11-01","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"One size fits all never fit anyone's period.","title":"One size fits all never fit anyone's period.","caption":"One size fits all never fit anyone's period.\n\nBodies are different, flows are different and days are different. Menstrual care should be built around that, not squeezed into a single shape.\n\nWhat do you wish pads came in? Tell me in the comments.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #PeriodTalk #CustomPads #ReusablePads","notes":"Use a tidy line-up of several different pad shapes.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: One size fits all never fit anyone's period.","slides":[],"imageText":"One size fits all never fit anyone's period."},{"id":"wp-script-49","ideaId":49,"week":4,"date":"2026-11-02","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"The question everyone asks quietly: do cloth pads smell?","title":"The question everyone asks quietly: do cloth pads smell?","caption":"The question everyone asks quietly: do cloth pads smell?\n\nWell-washed, fully dried pads shouldn't. The trick is what happens in the hours after you change: a quick cold rinse, airy storage and a thorough dry.\n\nSwipe for the routine, and send me any question you've been too shy to ask.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #PadCare #PeriodTalk","notes":"Check this matches your own washing instructions (cold rinse, fabric softener advice, drying) so your care card and posts agree.","confirmation":"Confirm all washing/storage advice against your own care card.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): The question everyone asks quietly: do cloth pads smell?\nSlide 2: The honest answer is that clean, well-washed pads shouldn't smell like anything. Most of the worry comes from not knowing what to do after you take one off.\nSlide 3: The smell people remember usually comes from leaving a used pad damp and sealed away for too long.\nSlide 4: So rinse it soon, in cold water, until the water runs mostly clear.\nSlide 5: Store used pads somewhere airy and dry until wash day, such as an open container or a wet bag you empty often.\nSlide 6: Wash them following the supplied care instructions, and make sure they dry completely. In humid Singapore, a breezy spot or a fan helps a lot.\nSlide 7: If a pad ever doesn't smell fresh, check your rinse and your drying first. If odour persists after washing and complete drying, check your detergent and care routine too.\nSlide 8: Got another question you're too shy to ask? Ask me, no judgement.","slides":[{"title":"The question everyone asks quietly: do cloth pads smell?","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"The honest answer is that clean, well-washed pads shouldn't smell like anything. Most of the worry comes from not knowing what to do after you take one off."},{"title":"02","body":"The smell people remember usually comes from leaving a used pad damp and sealed away for too long."},{"title":"03","body":"So rinse it soon, in cold water, until the water runs mostly clear."},{"title":"04","body":"Store used pads somewhere airy and dry until wash day, such as an open container or a wet bag you empty often."},{"title":"05","body":"Wash them following the supplied care instructions, and make sure they dry completely. In humid Singapore, a breezy spot or a fan helps a lot."},{"title":"06","body":"If a pad ever doesn't smell fresh, check your rinse and your drying first. If odour persists after washing and complete drying, check your detergent and care routine too."},{"title":"What would you like to know?","body":"Ask your cloth pad care questions at @ecoclothpad. Follow for more practical tips."}],"cta":"message"},{"id":"wp-script-42","ideaId":42,"week":4,"date":"2026-11-04","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Out and about with a used pad? Here's what to do.","title":"Out and about with a used pad? Here's what to do.","caption":"Out and about with a used pad? Here's what to do.\n\nFold it inwards so the soiled part is tucked away, then pop it into a small wet bag or a zipped pouch. Keep your clean spare in a separate clean pouch or compartment so your change is quick.\n\nWhen you get home, rinse it and wash following the supplied care instructions. That's all there is to it.\n\nSave this for your next day out.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #PadCare #PeriodTips","notes":"Add a photo of a pad folded in a wet bag.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Out and about with a used pad? / Fold it, wrap it, pop it in a wet bag.","slides":[],"imageText":"Out and about with a used pad? / Fold it, wrap it, pop it in a wet bag."},{"id":"wp-script-41","ideaId":41,"week":4,"date":"2026-11-06","format":"Reel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Washing cloth pads is easier than you think. Watch.","title":"Washing cloth pads is easier than you think. Watch.","caption":"Washing cloth pads is easier than you think. Watch.\n\nA cold rinse, a wash following your pad's care instructions and a thorough dry, and you're done. Rinsing is the hands-on part; washing and complete drying take longer. Follow the care instructions supplied with your pads.\n\nSend this to someone who's nervous about washing.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #PadCare #HowToWashClothPads","notes":"Match every step to your own care card. You can reuse clips from your washing guide carousel.","confirmation":"Confirm every washing step against your care card before filming.","script":"Length: 20 to 25 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: Used pad in the sink; cold tap running.\nOn screen: Washing cloth pads is easier than you think.\nVoiceover: Washing cloth pads is easier than you think. Let me show you.\nScene 2\nShot: Rinsing under cold water.\nOn screen: 1. Rinse in cold water.\nVoiceover: First, rinse it in cold water until it runs mostly clear.\nScene 3\nShot: Pads going into the washing machine.\nOn screen: 2. Follow your pad's washing instructions.\nVoiceover: Then it goes in with your wash using the supplied care instructions.\nScene 4\nShot: Pads on a drying rack or line.\nOn screen: 3. Dry completely.\nVoiceover: Then dry it completely, ideally somewhere airy or in the sun.\nScene 5\nShot: A stack of clean, folded pads.\nOn screen: Ready for next time.\nVoiceover: And that's it. Clean, folded and ready for next time.\nScene 6\nShot: Your Instagram handle: @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Questions? Ask me.\nVoiceover: Got a washing question? Ask me.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-103","ideaId":103,"week":4,"date":"2026-11-08","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"It's midnight, the machine is still humming, and your order is almost done.","title":"It's midnight, the machine is still humming, and your order is almost done.","caption":"It's midnight, the machine is still humming and your order is almost done.\n\nRunning a small business on your own means the sewing often happens when the house is finally quiet. It's tiring, but there's something lovely about knowing a pad I'm finishing tonight will soon be part of someone's everyday routine.\n\nSay hi if you're a night owl too.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #MakerLife #HandmadeInSingapore #SmallBusinessSG #BehindTheScenes","notes":"Use a photo of your sewing machine in warm lamp light with a half-finished pad. Keep it true to your own routine.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: It's midnight, the sewing machine is still going, and your order is almost done.","slides":[],"imageText":"It's midnight, the sewing machine is still going, and your order is almost done."},{"id":"wp-script-51","ideaId":51,"week":5,"date":"2026-11-09","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Can cloth pads leak? Honestly, yes. Here's why, and what helps.","title":"Can cloth pads leak? Honestly, yes. Here's why, and what helps.","caption":"Can cloth pads leak? Honestly, yes. Here's why, and what helps.\n\nAnyone who tells you a pad never leaks is selling you something. What matters is finding the cause: absorbency, length, fit or timing. Adjusting these can help reduce leaks.\n\nSave this, and message me if you'd like help troubleshooting yours.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #PadLeaks #ReusablePads #PeriodTips","notes":"","confirmation":"","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Can cloth pads leak? Honestly, yes. Here's why, and what helps.\nSlide 2: Any pad can leak, cloth or disposable, and it's rarely a sign that cloth pads don't work. It usually means something about the match needs adjusting.\nSlide 3: The most common cause is absorbency that's too light for your flow on that day.\nSlide 4: The next is length. If the pad doesn't cover enough at the front or back, the flow finds its way around it.\nSlide 5: Fit comes next. A pad that shifts or bunches can't protect as well as one that stays snug and comfortable.\nSlide 6: And sometimes it's simply time. On heavy days, changing a little earlier can make all the difference.\nSlide 7: So when a pad leaks, don't give up on cloth. Notice where and when it happened, and adjust one thing at a time.\nSlide 8: Stuck on a leak? Message @ecoclothpad what happened and we'll work out what to change.","slides":[{"title":"Can cloth pads leak? Honestly, yes. Here's why, and what helps.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"Any pad can leak, cloth or disposable, and it's rarely a sign that cloth pads don't work. It usually means something about the match needs adjusting."},{"title":"02","body":"The most common cause is absorbency that's too light for your flow on that day."},{"title":"03","body":"The next is length. If the pad doesn't cover enough at the front or back, the flow finds its way around it."},{"title":"04","body":"Fit comes next. A pad that shifts or bunches can't protect as well as one that stays snug and comfortable."},{"title":"05","body":"And sometimes it's simply time. On heavy days, changing a little earlier can make all the difference."},{"title":"06","body":"So when a pad leaks, don't give up on cloth. Notice where and when it happened, and adjust one thing at a time."},{"title":"Save this leak checklist","body":"Check absorbency, coverage, fit and timing. Message @ecoclothpad if you need help choosing a pad."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-112","ideaId":112,"week":5,"date":"2026-11-11","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Remember the classroom whisper? 'Do you have a pad?'","title":"Remember the classroom whisper? 'Do you have a pad?'","caption":"Remember the classroom whisper? 'Do you have a pad?'\n\nThe quiet question passed across a desk, the pad tucked into a sleeve or a pencil case, the hope that nobody noticed. Many of us learned very early that periods were something to be whispered about.\n\nI'd love for that to feel a little easier. Share your own classroom memory in the comments, if you'd like to.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #PeriodTalk #NormalisePeriods #ClothPadsSingapore #PeriodPositive","notes":"Add one line from your own school memory so it feels personal. Use a plain pink background and one small pad photo.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Remember the classroom whisper? / 'Do you have a pad?'","slides":[],"imageText":"Remember the classroom whisper? / 'Do you have a pad?'"},{"id":"wp-script-57","ideaId":57,"week":5,"date":"2026-11-13","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Sleeping in cloth pads: what works for overnight.","title":"Sleeping in cloth pads: what works for overnight.","caption":"Sleeping in cloth pads: what works for overnight.\n\nA long, absorbent, snug pad is the winning combination. Try your chosen pad at home to see whether it suits your overnight flow and comfort.\n\nMessage @ecoclothpad about overnight lengths and I'll help you choose.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #OvernightPads #ReusablePads #PeriodCare","notes":"Everyone's different. If you have a specific overnight size you recommend, add its name to slide 3.","confirmation":"Confirm your overnight pad guidance.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Sleeping in cloth pads: what works for overnight.\nSlide 2: Overnight is where many people feel most unsure about cloth, and it's also where the right pad makes the biggest difference.\nSlide 3: Go longer. You move a lot while you sleep, so extra length at the back and front gives you more coverage.\nSlide 4: Choose higher absorbency. Choose absorbency suited to your own overnight flow. A daytime light pad may not provide the protection you need.\nSlide 5: Pick a snug fit. A pad that stays in place as you turn over won't bunch or slip.\nSlide 6: Change just before bed and as soon as you wake up, so the pad starts and ends the night fresh.\nSlide 7: Give it a try at home first. Wearing one on a quiet weekend night is a lovely way to see how it feels.\nSlide 8: Want help choosing an overnight pad? Message @ecoclothpad.","slides":[{"title":"Sleeping in cloth pads: what works for overnight.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"Overnight is where many people feel most unsure about cloth, and it's also where the right pad makes the biggest difference."},{"title":"02","body":"Go longer. You move a lot while you sleep, so extra length at the back and front gives you more coverage."},{"title":"03","body":"Choose higher absorbency. Choose absorbency suited to your own overnight flow. A daytime light pad may not provide the protection you need."},{"title":"04","body":"Pick a snug fit. A pad that stays in place as you turn over won't bunch or slip."},{"title":"05","body":"Change just before bed and as soon as you wake up, so the pad starts and ends the night fresh."},{"title":"06","body":"Give it a try at home first. Wearing one on a quiet weekend night is a lovely way to see how it feels."},{"title":"Save this for your next overnight pad","body":"Choose coverage and absorbency that suit you. Explore the options at wonder-pads.com."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-102","ideaId":102,"week":5,"date":"2026-11-15","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Why your handmade pad takes time, not just a few minutes.","title":"Why your handmade pad takes time, not just a few minutes.","caption":"Why your handmade pad takes time, not just a few minutes.\n\nEvery pad is chosen, cut, layered, stitched and checked, one at a time. A custom pad adds the extra step of making it fit you. That's why it takes time, and why I think it's worth waiting for.\n\nThank you for being patient with a small maker.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #HandmadeInSingapore #BehindTheScenes #ClothPadsSingapore #SlowMade","notes":"Use a photo showing the stages: cut fabric, layers, stitching and a finished pad.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Why your handmade pad takes time, not just a few minutes.","slides":[],"imageText":"Why your handmade pad takes time, not just a few minutes."},{"id":"wp-script-68","ideaId":68,"week":6,"date":"2026-11-16","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"The easiest first step into reusables might not be a pad at all.","title":"The easiest first step into reusables might not be a pad at all.","caption":"The easiest first step into reusables might not be a pad at all.\n\nLiners are small, light and low-pressure. They let you learn the routine of wearing, rinsing and washing without committing to a full period.\n\nTell me if you'd start with a liner, or send me a message and I'll help you choose.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothLiners #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #BeginnerFriendly","notes":"Check slide 4 against what your own liners are designed for.","confirmation":"Confirm the uses and changing guidance for your liners.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): The easiest first step into reusables might not be a pad at all.\nSlide 2: If a full cloth pad feels like a big leap, a liner is a gentle way in.\nSlide 3: Liners are slim, light and quick to wash, which makes them easy to try on a normal day.\nSlide 4: They work for everyday discharge, spotting, light days and as backup to a cup.\nSlide 5: Because they're small, you can learn how washing and drying work with almost no effort.\nSlide 6: And once you're comfortable, moving up to a light pad is a natural next step.\nSlide 7: You don't need a big stash. How many you need depends on how often you change and how often you wash. Keep clean, dry spares ready.\nSlide 8: Curious? Message @ecoclothpad and I'll help you choose your first liner.","slides":[{"title":"The easiest first step into reusables might not be a pad at all.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"If a full cloth pad feels like a big leap, a liner is a gentle way in."},{"title":"02","body":"Liners are slim, light and quick to wash, which makes them easy to try on a normal day."},{"title":"03","body":"They work for everyday discharge, spotting, light days and as backup to a cup."},{"title":"04","body":"Because they're small, you can learn how washing and drying work with almost no effort."},{"title":"05","body":"And once you're comfortable, moving up to a light pad is a natural next step."},{"title":"06","body":"You don't need a big stash. How many you need depends on how often you change and how often you wash. Keep clean, dry spares ready."},{"title":"Would you start with a liner?","body":"Share your thoughts with @ecoclothpad. Explore liners at wonder-pads.com."}],"cta":"message"},{"id":"wp-script-61","ideaId":61,"week":6,"date":"2026-11-18","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"One little liner, so many different days.","title":"One little liner, so many different days.","caption":"One little liner, so many different days.\n\nEveryday discharge, spotting, very light days, backup for a cup, or a little extra reassurance. A single liner can cover all of it, and it washes in a moment.\n\nSave this for everyday ideas.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothLiners #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #EverydayCare","notes":"Use one liner photographed from above, with small icons for each use if you like.","confirmation":"Confirm these uses match your liners.","script":"Image text: One little liner. / So many different days.","slides":[],"imageText":"One little liner. / So many different days."},{"id":"wp-script-73","ideaId":73,"week":6,"date":"2026-11-20","format":"Reel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Your period at 25 isn't your period at 45, and your pads can change too.","title":"Your period at 25 isn't your period at 45, and your pads can change too.","caption":"Your period at 25 isn't your period at 45, and your pads can change too.\n\nNeeds shift through different seasons of life. A flexible set of liners and pads can follow you through them, so you're not stuck with something that no longer fits.\n\nShare this with someone who needs it.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ChangingNeeds #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusablePads #PeriodTalk","notes":"Check this against your finished perimenopause series so it doesn't repeat the same story. Check that this complements your existing series. Changes that concern you should be discussed with a healthcare professional.","confirmation":"","script":"Length: 25 to 30 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: Three pads in different sizes, lined up on pink.\nOn screen: Your period at 25 isn't your period at 45.\nVoiceover: Your period at twenty-five isn't your period at forty-five.\nScene 2\nShot: Hand moves from the smallest pad to the biggest.\nOn screen: Needs change over time.\nVoiceover: Flow can change, cycles can change, and what felt perfect once may stop working.\nScene 3\nShot: Hand picks up a liner and a light pad.\nOn screen: Some days, you may need lighter protection.\nVoiceover: Some days you may need lighter protection, and on others you need more absorbency.\nScene 4\nShot: Hand picks up a longer, more absorbent pad.\nOn screen: Some months, you need more.\nVoiceover: And on other days, you want a longer, more absorbent pad.\nScene 5\nShot: Pads all together.\nOn screen: Your pads can change with you.\nVoiceover: That's the beauty of reusables: you can build a small set that changes with you.\nScene 6\nShot: Your Instagram handle: @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Share this with someone who needs it.\nVoiceover: Share this with someone who needs to hear it.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-106","ideaId":106,"week":6,"date":"2026-11-22","format":"Reel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Packing orders: the tiny ritual that makes my day.","title":"Packing orders: the tiny ritual that makes my day.","caption":"Packing orders: the tiny ritual that makes my day.\n\nIt's quiet, a little repetitive and surprisingly lovely. Each parcel leaves with a small piece of me inside it.\n\nTell me what you'd put in your first order.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #BehindTheScenes #HandmadeInSingapore #SmallBusinessSG #ClothPadsSingapore","notes":"A short phone clip is enough. Don't show addresses or customer names on parcels.","confirmation":"","script":"Length: 15 to 20 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: Close-up of a finished pad on the table.\nOn screen: Packing orders.\nVoiceover: This is my favourite quiet moment of the day.\nScene 2\nShot: Hands wrapping the pad in tissue.\nOn screen: Wrapped with care.\nVoiceover: Every pad gets wrapped with care.\nScene 3\nShot: Sealing the envelope or box.\nOn screen: One order at a time.\nVoiceover: Sealed up, one order at a time.\nScene 4\nShot: A stack of parcels ready to go.\nOn screen: On its way to you.\nVoiceover: And off it goes to someone I've never met, but already care about.\nScene 5\nShot: @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Tell me what you'd put in your first order.\nVoiceover: Tell me what you'd put in your first order.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-78","ideaId":78,"week":7,"date":"2026-11-23","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Let's do the maths: disposable versus reusable, over a few years.","title":"Let's do the maths: disposable versus reusable, over a few years.","caption":"Let's do the maths: disposable versus reusable, over a few years.\n\nIt's easy to look at the price of a set of cloth pads and think it's a lot. It's less obvious that a pack of disposables every month adds up to a lot too, and never stops.\n\nSave this and do your own sums. If you'd like help, message @ecoclothpad.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #ReusableSavings #SustainableLivingSG #ReusablePads","notes":"IMPORTANT: replace every [bracketed] number with your real SGD prices before posting. Don't use made-up figures.","confirmation":"Replace all bracketed quantities/prices with your real SGD figures and review the comparison assumptions.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Let's do the maths: disposable versus reusable, over a few years.\nSlide 2: Disposable pads feel cheap because you buy them one pack at a time. But a pack every month adds up quickly.\nSlide 3: Say you spend about $[your monthly disposable spend] a month. Over a year, that's $[monthly x 12], and over three years, $[monthly x 36].\nSlide 4: A reusable set costs more at the start. A set of [number] pads comes to about $[your set price] once.\nSlide 5: And with proper care, a good cloth pad can be used again and again for years.\nSlide 6: Over a few years, the gap can be big. Spread your spend over time and a reusable set often comes out ahead.\nSlide 7: This isn't about being perfect. Even replacing part of your disposable use makes a difference to your wallet.\nSlide 8: Want to work out your own numbers? Message @ecoclothpad and we'll do the sums together.","slides":[{"title":"Let's do the maths: disposable versus reusable, over a few years.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"Disposable pads feel cheap because you buy them one pack at a time. But a pack every month adds up quickly."},{"title":"02","body":"Say you spend about $[your monthly disposable spend] a month. Over a year, that's $[monthly x 12], and over three years, $[monthly x 36]."},{"title":"03","body":"A reusable set costs more at the start. A set of [number] pads comes to about $[your set price] once."},{"title":"04","body":"And with proper care, a good cloth pad can be used again and again for years."},{"title":"05","body":"Over a few years, the gap can be big. Spread your spend over time and a reusable set often comes out ahead."},{"title":"06","body":"This isn't about being perfect. Even replacing part of your disposable use makes a difference to your wallet."},{"title":"Save this and do your own sums","body":"Use your actual prices, changing routine and care costs. Explore your options at wonder-pads.com."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-88","ideaId":88,"week":7,"date":"2026-11-25","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"There is no backup planet. Let's talk about small changes.","title":"There is no backup planet. Let's talk about small changes.","caption":"There is no backup planet. Let's talk about small changes.\n\nI don't think any of us can fix everything, and I don't think we have to. But small, repeated habits do add up, and a reusable pad is one of the small things you can choose.\n\nShare one small habit you've changed lately.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #SustainableLivingSG #ReusablePads #SmallChangesMatter #ClothPadsSingapore","notes":"Use a quiet photo of greenery or a window, with the line over it in handwriting.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: There is no backup planet.","slides":[],"imageText":"There is no backup planet."},{"id":"wp-script-91","ideaId":91,"week":7,"date":"2026-11-27","format":"Reel","effort":"Heavy","hook":"A bin full of used pads, or a bin full of money?","title":"A bin full of used pads, or a bin full of money?","caption":"A bin full of used pads, or a bin full of money?\n\nWe rarely think about what we throw away because it's out of sight the moment the lid closes. But the waste and the cost both pile up all the same.\n\nSend this to someone who loves a good comparison.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #SustainableLivingSG #ReusablePads #ClothPadsSingapore #ZeroWasteSG","notes":"Plan the shot first. Use clean props only, such as unused pad packaging or paper, never anything soiled.","confirmation":"","script":"Length: 20 to 25 seconds\nScene 1\nShot: A small bin full of used disposable pads (use clean props, packaging only).\nOn screen: A bin full of used pads...\nVoiceover: Imagine your bin at the end of a year of disposable pads.\nScene 2\nShot: A jar or bowl of coins and notes beside it.\nOn screen: ...or a bin full of money?\nVoiceover: Now imagine that same pile as money.\nScene 3\nShot: Hands drop a coin into the jar.\nOn screen: Every pad you don't throw out...\nVoiceover: Every disposable pad you replace is one less in the bin.\nScene 4\nShot: The jar filling up.\nOn screen: ...stays in your pocket.\nVoiceover: And a little more stays in your pocket.\nScene 5\nShot: A stack of clean folded cloth pads.\nOn screen: Reusable adds up.\nVoiceover: That's the quiet maths of reusable.\nScene 6\nShot: @ecoclothpad.\nOn screen: Send this to someone who loves a good comparison.\nVoiceover: Send this to someone who loves a good comparison.","slides":[],"imageText":""},{"id":"wp-script-93","ideaId":93,"week":7,"date":"2026-11-29","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Sustainable doesn't mean perfect.","title":"Sustainable doesn't mean perfect.","caption":"Sustainable doesn't mean perfect.\n\nYou can use cloth pads some days and disposables on others. You can buy fewer things but still treat yourself. What counts is a choice you can realistically keep making, not a guilt trip.\n\nShare this if it feels like a relief.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #SustainableLivingSG #ReusablePads #NoGuiltTrips #ClothPadsSingapore","notes":"","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: Sustainable doesn't mean perfect.","slides":[],"imageText":"Sustainable doesn't mean perfect."},{"id":"wp-script-35","ideaId":35,"week":8,"date":"2026-11-30","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"AIO or exposed-core? Here's the difference in plain words.","title":"AIO or exposed-core? Here's the difference in plain words.","caption":"AIO or exposed-core? Here's the difference in plain words.\n\nThe names sound technical, but the idea is simple. It's about how the absorbent layers are built in, and how that affects the way a pad washes, dries and feels.\n\nSave this before you order, and message me if you'd like help choosing.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #AIOPads #ReusablePads #PadConstruction","notes":"IMPORTANT: confirm slides 3 and 4 match exactly how YOU make your AIO and exposed-core pads (and how they dry) before posting.","confirmation":"Confirm the AIO and exposed-core descriptions match your actual construction.","script":"Slide 1 (cover): AIO or exposed-core? Here's the difference in plain words.\nSlide 2: You'll see these two terms a lot when you look at cloth pads. They describe how the absorbent layers are built into the pad.\nSlide 3: An all-in-one pad, or AIO, has its absorbent core enclosed inside the pad's fabric, so everything sits neatly in one piece.\nSlide 4: An exposed-core pad has the absorbent core visible, which can change how it dries and how the edges look and feel.\nSlide 5: Both can be comfortable and effective. They're simply two ways of building a pad.\nSlide 6: Which is better for you depends on how you like to wash, dry and wear your pads.\nSlide 7: If you're not sure, don't worry. I'll explain what each option means for the pad you want.\nSlide 8: Questions about construction? Message @ecoclothpad and I'll walk you through it.","slides":[{"title":"AIO or exposed-core? Here's the difference in plain words.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"You'll see these two terms a lot when you look at cloth pads. They describe how the absorbent layers are built into the pad."},{"title":"02","body":"An all-in-one pad, or AIO, has its absorbent core enclosed inside the pad's fabric, so everything sits neatly in one piece."},{"title":"03","body":"An exposed-core pad has the absorbent core visible, which can change how it dries and how the edges look and feel."},{"title":"04","body":"Both can be comfortable and effective. They're simply two ways of building a pad."},{"title":"05","body":"Which is better for you depends on how you like to wash, dry and wear your pads."},{"title":"06","body":"If you're not sure, don't worry. I'll explain what each option means for the pad you want."},{"title":"Save this before you order","body":"Keep this guide handy. Message @ecoclothpad about the construction options available."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-107","ideaId":107,"week":8,"date":"2026-12-02","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"When you reorder, a small maker does a little happy dance.","title":"When you reorder, a small maker does a little happy dance.","caption":"When you reorder, a small maker does a little happy dance.\n\nWhen someone comes back for another pad, it tells me the first one worked for them. For a business that's just me, there's no better feeling.\n\nThank you to everyone who has ever come back for more.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ThankYou #SmallBusinessSG #HandmadeInSingapore #ClothPadsSingapore","notes":"Use a photo of ready-to-post parcels with a handwritten thank-you note.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: When you reorder, a small maker does a little happy dance.","slides":[],"imageText":"When you reorder, a small maker does a little happy dance."},{"id":"wp-script-132","ideaId":132,"week":8,"date":"2026-12-04","format":"Carousel","effort":"Medium","hook":"Not sure where to start? How to choose your first Wonder Pad.","title":"Not sure where to start? How to choose your first Wonder Pad.","caption":"Not sure where to start? Here's how to choose your first Wonder Pad.\n\nYou don't need to know everything. Start with your flow, when you'll wear it and how much coverage you want, then pick a fabric you love. I'll help with the rest.\n\nPin this one, and Message @ecoclothpad when you're ready to begin.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #FirstClothPad #CustomPads #ReusablePads","notes":"Pin this to your profile. Add your real pad names to slides 2 to 5 if you want it to be product-specific.","confirmation":"","script":"Slide 1 (cover): Not sure where to start? How to choose your first Wonder Pad.\nSlide 2: Start with your flow. Is it light, moderate or heavy on most days? That decides the absorbency you'll want.\nSlide 3: Then think about when you'll wear it. Daytime at home, a busy day out and a long night's sleep each want something a little different.\nSlide 4: Pick a length. Longer gives more coverage, and shorter is easier for everyday wear.\nSlide 5: Choose a shape you feel comfortable in. Some people like more coverage and some like to keep it slim.\nSlide 6: Then the fun part: choose your fabric. Soft, pretty and yours.\nSlide 7: If you're not sure, start with one pad and one liner. You can build from there once you know what you like.\nSlide 8: Not sure about any of this? Message @ecoclothpad and we'll pick your first Wonder Pad together.","slides":[{"title":"Not sure where to start? How to choose your first Wonder Pad.","body":""},{"title":"01","body":"Start with your flow. Is it light, moderate or heavy on most days? That decides the absorbency you'll want."},{"title":"02","body":"Then think about when you'll wear it. Daytime at home, a busy day out and a long night's sleep each want something a little different."},{"title":"03","body":"Pick a length. Longer gives more coverage, and shorter is easier for everyday wear."},{"title":"04","body":"Choose a shape you feel comfortable in. Some people like more coverage and some like to keep it slim."},{"title":"05","body":"Then the fun part: choose your fabric. Soft, pretty and yours."},{"title":"06","body":"If you're not sure, start with one pad and one liner. You can build from there once you know what you like."},{"title":"Save your first-pad checklist","body":"Keep this guide handy and explore wonder-pads.com. Message @ecoclothpad for help choosing."}],"cta":"save"},{"id":"wp-script-109","ideaId":109,"week":8,"date":"2026-12-06","format":"Static post","effort":"Quick","hook":"Enough talking. Here are the real pads.","title":"Enough talking. Here are the real pads.","caption":"Enough talking. Here are the real pads.\n\nAfter weeks of explaining flow, length, fabric and care, here they are in all their colourful glory, made by hand and ready to be someone's new favourite.\n\nMessage @ecoclothpad if you'd like to see more in person.","hashtags":"#WonderPadsSG #ClothPadsSingapore #HandmadeInSingapore #CustomPads #ReusablePads","notes":"Use your best flat-lay of real pads, with no text on the image.","confirmation":"","script":"Image text: (No text. Let the pads speak.)","slides":[],"imageText":""}];
